==French==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fr|frm|amuser||to amuse, divert, babble}}, from {{inh|fr|fro|amuser||to stupefy, waste time, be lost in thought}}, from {{m|fro|a-}} + {{m|fro|muser||to stare stupidly at, gape, wander, waste time, loiter, think carefully about, attend to}}, of uncertain and obscure origin. Cognate with {{cog|oc|musa||idle waiting}}, {{cog|it|musare||to gape idly about}}. Possibly from {{cog|fro|*mus||snout}} from {{inh|fr|VL.|*mūsa||snout}} (compare {{cog|ML.|mūsum||muzzle, snout}}), from {{der|fr|gem-pro|*mū-||muzzle, snout}}, from {{der|fr|ine-pro|*mū-||lips, muzzle}}. Compare {{cog|de|Maul||muzzle, snout}}.

An alternative etymology connects {{cog|fro|muser}} and {{cog|oc|musa}} with {{der|fr|goh|muoza||careful attention, leisure, idleness}}, from {{der|fr|gem-pro|*mōtǭ||leave, permission}}, from {{der|fr|ine-pro|*med-||to acquire, possess, control}}. Compare also {{cog|goh|muozōn||to be idle, have leisure or opportunity}}, {{cog|de|Muße||leisure}}. More at {{l|en|empty}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|Fr-amuser.ogg|Audio|lang=fr}}

